From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: gc8613: accept a 1% xclk window on T41

The T41 CIM MCLK divider can resolve to 27 MHz (VPLL / 44) or 26.926 MHz
(APLL / 41) depending on which parent the mux picks. The 0.27% error is
inside the sensor's xclk tolerance, so accept a 1% window instead of
requiring an exact rate.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/gc8613.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc8613.c
@@ -752,7 +752,13 @@
 				     "failed to get xclk\n");
 
 	xclk_freq = clk_get_rate(gc8613->xclk);
-	if (xclk_freq != GC8613_XCLK_FREQ)
+	/*
+	 * The stock CIM mux uses VPLL / 44 = 27 MHz; a different parent
+	 * selection can leave APLL / 41 = 26.926 MHz. The 0.27% error is
+	 * inside the sensor's xclk tolerance, so accept a 1% window.
+	 */
+	if (xclk_freq < GC8613_XCLK_FREQ - GC8613_XCLK_FREQ / 100 ||
+	    xclk_freq > GC8613_XCLK_FREQ + GC8613_XCLK_FREQ / 100)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL,
 				     "xclk frequency %lu Hz not supported\n",
 				     xclk_freq);
